OrionLayer open fix 124 — g_injected_mouse_pending is a std::atomic<bool>
=========================================================================

Work order 437 (parity audit of 25 November 2026, finding F-04). orion2re on the
fork's branch `orionlayer` (v2.0.1), after open fix 123. Not on
`orionlayer-local`. In src/ext/ext_api.h and src/ext/ext_api.cpp.

g_injected_mouse_pending (open fix 3) is set by ProcessInput
(ext_api.cpp, the injected clicks and FilmGuard) and cleared by
Pump_Game_Input_Queue (platform.cpp, from Pointer_X, Pointer_Y and the main
loop) - the game thread, MOX2::main2, created with SDL_CreateThread in
platform.cpp - and READ by Sync_Mouse_State_From_SDL, which the SDL event
loop of the main thread calls (focus gained, F10, a fullscreen toggle). Two
threads, a plain bool: a data race. g_hide_window got std::atomic in open
fix 43; this flag did not.

The change. `extern std::atomic<bool>` in the header, `std::atomic<bool>
g_injected_mouse_pending{false}` in the definition. <atomic> was already
included. platform.cpp is untouched: `if (flag)` and `flag = false` compile
against an atomic unchanged. Same ordering (the default, sequentially
consistent) as g_hide_window.

Proved: ext_api.cpp and platform.cpp syntax-checked on the scratch clone with
the build's own flags and PCH (ORION2RE_EXT on), a misspelt use refused; the
branch built with `cmake --build --preset linux-debug`. Live: UNVERIFIED, see
doc/orion2re_open_fixes.md entry 124.

